AIX FUSE licensing
==================

This repository combines components under two licenses:

- LICENSE.LGPL-2.1-only contains the complete GNU Lesser General Public
  License, version 2.1 only, for the adapted libfuse headers and code.
- LICENSE.MIT contains the MIT copyright and permission notice for original
  MIT-licensed adapter components, examples, tests, and supporting files.
  The bundled native USFS client also retains its own MIT license notice.

These licenses apply to their respective components. They are not a choice
of alternative licenses for the entire project. Per-file SPDX identifiers
and copyright notices describe the component boundaries.

The combined libfuse3.a library contains components under both MIT and
LGPL-2.1-only. As a combined library it is governed by LGPL-2.1-only as a
whole, while its MIT-licensed components retain their MIT copyright and
permission notices and remain available separately under MIT. Compliance with
both sets of applicable notices is required; the combined library is not
offered under MIT alone. RPM metadata is therefore MIT AND LGPL-2.1-only.

The RPM's aix_fuse_mirror and aix_fuse_memfs executables are statically linked
with libfuse3.a. Each executable uses the LGPL-covered library, and the library
and its use in the executable are covered by LGPL-2.1-only. The accompanying
source.tar.gz contains the corresponding library source and the MIT-licensed
source for both executables so recipients can modify the library and relink
the executables.

The RPM includes both full license texts and this explanation. It also
preserves the selected native USFS snapshot's notice as LICENSE.native-usfs,
with the original retained at bundled/usfs/LICENSE in the corresponding
source archive. That copy preserves dependency attribution; it does not
introduce a third license.
